extends layout

block styles
  link(rel='stylesheet', href='/css/connectivityDashboard.css')

block content
  main.connectivity-page
    header.connectivity-header
      div
        p.connectivity-eyebrow SYSTEM OBSERVATIONS
        h1 Connectivity analytics
        p Compare outbound HTTPS, public app readiness, local health, and MongoDB ping.
        a#performance-link(href='/admin/performance?range=24') Compare app performance
        |  ·
        a(href='/admin/connectivity/api') Raw history JSON
      .connectivity-controls
        label(for='connectivity-window') Time window
        select#connectivity-window
          option(value='1') Last hour
          option(value='6') Last 6 hours
          option(value='24', selected) Last 24 hours
          option(value='72') Last 72 hours
        button#connectivity-refresh(type='button') Refresh
    p#connectivity-message(role='status', aria-live='polite') Loading stored observations…
    noscript This dashboard needs JavaScript. The raw history JSON link remains available.
    #connectivity-results(hidden)
      section.connectivity-summary(aria-label='Observation summary')
        article
          h2 Recent external status
          strong#recent-status
          p#latest-at
        article
          h2 Sample coverage
          strong#coverage-value
          p#coverage-detail
        article
          h2 Alert attempts
          strong#alert-value
          p#alert-detail
      p#config-note.connectivity-note
      section(aria-labelledby='probe-heading')
        h2#probe-heading Probe reliability and latency
        p Percentages describe stored samples, never continuous uptime. Successful responses include slow successes; timeouts and failed contracts are excluded from latency percentiles.
        #probe-cards.connectivity-cards
      section(aria-labelledby='timeline-heading')
        h2#timeline-heading Aligned observation timeline
        p#timeline-range
        p Each column covers the same time on every row. A colored cell contains observations, not proof of health throughout that time. Mixed cells show the worst observed state; empty cells are unknown.
        #timeline-legend.connectivity-legend
        #timeline.connectivity-timeline
        p#timeline-selection(role='status', aria-live='polite') Select a timeline cell to inspect its counts. A detailed history table is below.
      section(aria-labelledby='latency-heading')
        h2#latency-heading Successful-response latency
        p Bin p95 in milliseconds, aligned to the timeline above. Missing successes break the line. Failure duration is only shown in history.
        #latency-chart.connectivity-timeline
      section(aria-labelledby='dns-heading')
        h2#dns-heading DNS vs post-DNS latency
        p Successful-response bin p95 in milliseconds, using the same time columns above. Each target has its own scale, shared by its two lines. Select an observation timeline cell for exact values and sample counts.
        .connectivity-timing-legend(aria-label='Timing series')
          span.timing-dnsMs DNS · solid amber
          span.timing-postDnsMs Post-DNS · dashed aqua
        #dns-chart.connectivity-timeline
        p DNS is elapsed time from probe start to completed IPv4 A-record resolution. Post-DNS is stored total minus DNS for each successful sample, including connection, TLS, headers, body and validation. Percentiles are then calculated from those individual durations; the two p95 lines must not be added together.
        p Missing, invalid or inapplicable timings are unknown, never zero; missing values break each line independently. Cards show p50 / p95 and n (usable successful samples) for each duration. Older records may have total latency without a DNS breakdown. Failures and timeouts appear only in observation details, not these percentiles.
        details
          summary How connection and response durations are calculated
          p All values are milliseconds. Stored DNS, TCP, TLS and response-header (ttfbMs) values are cumulative monotonic milestones from probe start. TCP duration = TCP − DNS; TLS = TLS − TCP; wait for headers = response headers − TLS; body / validation = total − response headers. These approximate intervals include scheduling overhead and are not isolated server processing times. Each duration needs its recorded boundaries; per-phase sample counts may differ.
          p Timeout details use the recorded failure phase and, when its boundary is known, total elapsed minus that boundary. This is time spent up to failure, not a completed phase or proof of its root cause. Contract-validation start is not recorded, so its timeout duration is unknown. Event-loop stalls may delay milestones and deadlines.
      section(aria-labelledby='incidents-heading')
        h2#incidents-heading Observed degraded stretches
        p Successive slow or failing observations of one probe, ending at recovery, a gap, a configuration change, or the window boundary. Durations between samples are inferred; a single observation has no measured duration.
        #incidents.connectivity-table-wrap
      section(aria-labelledby='gaps-heading')
        h2#gaps-heading Observation gaps
        p Gaps exceed 1.5 sampling intervals, including window boundaries. They may reflect downtime, database write loss, a disabled collector, or retention. Missing observations never mean healthy.
        #gaps.connectivity-table-wrap
      section(aria-labelledby='alerts-heading')
        h2#alerts-heading Alert activity
        p Only the external probes drive alerts. Attempted means delivery is unknown; failed attempts consume cooldown. Local health and DB ping never trigger Pushover.
        #alerts.connectivity-table-wrap
      section(aria-labelledby='history-heading')
        h2#history-heading Recent observation details
        p#history-caption
        #history.connectivity-table-wrap
        .connectivity-controls
          button#history-previous(type='button') Newer
          button#history-next(type='button') Older
          a#history-raw-older(href='/admin/connectivity/api', hidden) Older raw details (paginated JSON)
      section.connectivity-note(aria-labelledby='limits-heading')
        h2#limits-heading What these measurements can tell us
        p Cloudflare edge connectivity does not test the Docker tunnel. HTTP 404/502 or a contract error proves an HTTP response arrived; it does not mean internet loss. The internet probe only measures one independent provider.
        p LOCAL health calls the existing unauthenticated /apphealth over loopback on this process’s actual listener. It checks MongoDB readiness only. DB ping is a separate real command with a maximum two-second budget, including driver selection and pool wait. Neither measures a typical application query.
        p External DNS, TCP, TLS, first-byte and total timings are cumulative monotonic milestones from request start. Missing phases are unknown or inapplicable. These small IPv4 requests use fresh connections and no retries; they do not reproduce your browser, bandwidth, Wi-Fi, IPv6, or all application routes.
        p Healthy local checks alongside external failures support investigating the outbound/public path, but cannot identify DNS, ISP, Cloudflare or tunnel as the cause. Event-loop stalls can delay timers too. Compare app performance timestamps and capture a slow browser request and Docker tunnel observations when needed.

block script
  script(src='/js/connectivityDashboard.js', defer)
